## Why This Is Asked
This checks understanding of test isolation and determinism in E2E tests using mocks for external services.

## Key Concepts
- Data seeding and reset for repeatable tests
- Network interception and mocked APIs
- End-to-end flow verification and backend validation
- CI reliability and speed trade-offs

## Code Example
```javascript
// Playwright test sketch
test('checkout end-to-end', async ({ page }) => {
  await page.route('**/payments', route => route.fulfill({ status: 200, body: JSON.stringify({ status:'success', id:'PAY123' }) }));
  await page.request.post('https://test.api/reset-db', { data: { seed: 'default' } });
  await page.goto('https://shop.example.com/product/1');
  await page.click('text=Add to cart');
  await page.goto('https://shop.example.com/checkout');
  await page.fill('#name', 'Test User');
  await page.fill('#address', '123 Main St');
  await page.click('text=Pay');
  await page.locator('text=Order Confirmed').waitFor();
  // backend verification
  const res = await page.request.get('https://test.api/orders/123');
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you adapt this test for a flaky payment API?
- What metrics would you collect to monitor CI stability for this flow?

